## [Microservices architecture on AWS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/simple-microservices-architecture-on-aws.md)

- [User interface](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/user-interface.md): Static web content can be served using Amazon S3 and Amazon CloudFront.
- [Microservices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/microservices.md): APIs manage and process client calls, and functions like traffic management, request filtering, routing, caching, authentication, and authorization.
- [CI/CD](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/continuous-integration-and-continuous-deployment-cicd.md): Continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) is a crucial part of a DevOps initiative for rapid software changes.
- [Private networking](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/private-networking.md): AWS PrivateLink enhances microservice security by allowing private connections between your Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and supported AWS services.
- [Data store](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/data-store.md): Popular stores for session data are in-memory caches such as Memcached or Redis.
- [Simplifying operations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/simplyfing-operations.md): To further simplify the operational efforts needed to run, maintain, and monitor microservices, we can use a fully serverless architecture.


## [Observability](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/observability.md)

- [Monitoring](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/monitoring.md): CloudWatch offers system-wide visibility into resource utilization, application performance, and operational health.
- [Centralizing logs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/centralizing-logs.md): Logging is key to pinpoint and resolve issues.
- [Distributed tracing](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/distributed-tracing.md): AWS X-Ray uses correlation IDs to track requests across these services.
- [Log analysis on AWS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/log-analysis-on-aws.md): Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights allows for real-time log exploration, analysis, and visualization.
- [Other options for analysis](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/microservices-on-aws/other-options-for-analysis.md): For further log analysis, Amazon Redshift, a fully-managed data warehouse service, and Quick, a scalable business intelligence service, offer effective solutions.


